<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat-Spring and white bids down.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat-Spring and white bids down.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dark northern spring wheat and soft white values weakened on Wednesday in line with lower spring wheat futures prices.</p>
<p>Grain prices fell sharply after the U.S. Department of Agriculture's monthly supply/demand report was bearishly-construed for wheat and feedgrains.</p>
<p>December MGE spring wheat futures lost 14 cents to finish at $4.20 a bushel.</p>
<p>Dealers noted that movement remained very slow. &quot;U.S. farmers do not want to sell but the rest of the world wants to come in (and sell their wheat),&quot; a Minnesota dealer said.</p>
<p>Another Montana dealer agreed that country sales were lackluster. &quot;Nobody is selling,&quot; he said.  </p>
